  "notes": "{呻|うめ}く describes making a low, involuntary sound of pain, distress, or anguish. Godan く-verb.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{呻|うめ}いている means \"is groaning\" — an ongoing action, not a resulting state.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {痛|いた}みで{呻|うめ}く: to groan in pain\n- {呻|うめ}き{声|ごえ}: a groan, moaning voice\n- {呻|うめ}き{続|つづ}ける: to keep groaning\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {呻|うめ}く: a low, involuntary sound of pain or anguish (softer)\n- {唸|うな}る: to groan, growl, or roar (stronger, more forceful — also used for animals)\n- {泣|な}く: to cry (tears, not just sound)\n\nREGISTER:\nCommon in literary and narrative writing. The kanji {呻|うめ} is uncommon; hiragana うめく is also used.",
